* Silicon microring bank, part 3: two self-pulsing rings in sequence on one bus at 7 mW, periodic
* or chaotic, and a twin of each started with 1 part in 1e9 more laser power.
*
* Each bank: the laser, ring A (as in ringchaos_bistable.net), then ring B on the same bus, driven
* by the field ring A lets through. The laser sits 10 linewidths red of both cold resonances.
*   bank 1 (+ twin 2): ring B identical to ring A. The two pulse in lock: periodic.
*   bank 3 (+ twin 4): ring B with a slower thermal time constant (260 ns, a larger or
*     differently clad ring), so it would pulse at its own, lower frequency: driven by ring A's
*     pulsing at an incommensurate ratio, the bank is chaotic. Checked over 300 us: about 300
*     distinct maxima in every 50 us, main and twin alike. (At 8 mW the same bank is chaotic only
*     for its first 50-125 us, then settles: transient chaos. The power matters.)
* The twins measure sensitivity to initial conditions. A periodic bank and its twin settle on the
* same orbit, at most shifted in time (the phase of an autonomous oscillation is free); a chaotic
* one separates exponentially, at roughly the largest Lyapunov exponent, until the two are
* uncorrelated. The return map of successive maxima (each against the next) shows the difference
* at a glance: a few points for a periodic orbit, a folded set of curves for the chaotic one.
* Reference: the largest Lyapunov exponent of the same equations, by the Benettin method
* (ringchaos_plots.py --lyapunov, about 1.5 hours), and the periodic bank's period, integrated
* with scipy.
* What to look for (measured at 2.16.2+6): bank 1 periodic, 8 distinct maxima, an interval of
* 25.062 ns between large peaks (scipy 25.118 ns), through power 1.4394-6.9192 mW (scipy
* 1.4386-6.9192); bank 3 chaotic, 290 distinct maxima in 50 us, its twin separating at ~1.3e6 /s
* and uncorrelated after 10 us; the Benettin exponent of the same equations is 1.36e6 /s over
* 100 us (still settling: 1.86, 1.67, 1.46e6 at 25, 50, 75 us; positive throughout).
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/ringchaos_bank.net --model models/multiphysics/ringchaos --tran --report o1,o2,o3,o4
VW wctl gnd DC 1550.155016
VP1 p1 gnd PWL(0 0 20n 7)
VP2 p2 gnd PWL(0 0 20n 7.000000007)
VP3 p3 gnd PWL(0 0 20n 7)
VP4 p4 gnd PWL(0 0 20n 7.000000007)
XL1 p1 wctl a0r a0i wl1 laser
XA1 a0r a0i a1r a1i wl1 ta1 siring
XB1 a1r a1i a2r a2i wl1 tb1 siring
XD1 a2r a2i o1 detector
XL2 p2 wctl b0r b0i wl2 laser
XA2 b0r b0i b1r b1i wl2 ta2 siring
XB2 b1r b1i b2r b2i wl2 tb2 siring
XD2 b2r b2i o2 detector
XL3 p3 wctl c0r c0i wl3 laser
XA3 c0r c0i c1r c1i wl3 ta3 siring
XB3 c1r c1i c2r c2i wl3 tb3 siring tth=260n
XD3 c2r c2i o3 detector
XL4 p4 wctl d0r d0i wl4 laser
XA4 d0r d0i d1r d1i wl4 ta4 siring
XB4 d1r d1i d2r d2i wl4 tb4 siring tth=260n
XD4 d2r d2i o4 detector
.tran 0.2n 60u
.end
